Z||000030||FieroMaster88||10-13-2001||04:38 PM||||Ok...not to keep kicking a dead horse or anything...but if the intake I made is contracting when it gets warm...why did the GM engineers use it on the car?   All I used was the stock tube that goes from the plenum to the air box....but used a cone filter instead of the air box!  So if it contracts when it heats up GM engineers don't know anything. <P>Heat shrink tubing is made from a different material than rubber.  Why would GM put heat shrink tubing on their intake that goes <B>OVER</B> the exhaust pipe?  That would be just plane stupid! <P>Also...does your radiator tube expand or contract when it gets warm????  Just a question.  If it contracted, even the pressure (15psi) of the coolant would not be able to keep it the same size as when it is cold.  I am not trying to piss anyone off...I just don't care too much for people who think they know everything so they have to try and point out how "stupid" others are.<BR>||||reg||1
